{"title":"Career Roadmap · Groundwater Engineer","role":"Groundwater Engineer","summary":"A Groundwater Engineer studies, assesses, develops and manages water stored beneath the Earth's surface. The role combines hydrogeology, geology, fluid mechanics, groundwater modelling, well engineering, geophysics, GIS, water-quality assessment and water-resource management.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Tech / B.E. (Bachelor of Technology / Engineering)","Course":"Geological / Applied Geology Engineering"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career Overview"},{"type":"p","text":"A Groundwater Engineer studies, assesses, develops and manages water stored beneath the Earth's surface. The role combines hydrogeology, geology, fluid mechanics, groundwater modelling, well engineering, geophysics, GIS, water-quality assessment and water-resource management."},{"type":"p","text":"Typical responsibilities include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Aquifer characterization"},{"text":"Groundwater exploration"},{"text":"Well-site assessment"},{"text":"Aquifer testing"},{"text":"Groundwater modelling"},{"text":"Recharge assessment"},{"text":"Groundwater-resource estimation"},{"text":"Contamination assessment"},{"text":"Well design and development"},{"text":"Groundwater monitoring"},{"text":"Artificial recharge planning"},{"text":"Sustainable groundwater management"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Core Career Positioning"},{"type":"flow","items":["Hydrogeology","Geology","Fluid Mechanics","Aquifer Analysis","Groundwater Modelling","Geophysics","GIS","Water Quality","Field Investigation"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Career Flow"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Tech / B.E.","Geology + Hydrology Fundamentals","Hydrogeology + Fluid Mechanics","Aquifers + Groundwater Flow","Field Investigation + Geophysics","Well Testing + Water Quality","GIS + Groundwater Modelling","Resource Assessment","Recharge / Contamination / Well Mana